/* book Worked example: Q: An InSb Hall plate has Hall coefficient RH = 3.8 × 10⁻⁴ m³/C and thickness t = 0.1 mm. A control current I = 10 mA flows while the plate sits in a flux density B = 0.2 T. (a) Find the Hall voltage VH. (b) Find the sensitivity in volts per tesla.
   1. Convert to SI units: t = 0.1 mm = 1 × 10⁻⁴ m; I = 10 mA = 0.01 A.
   2. VH = RH I B / t = (3.8 × 10⁻⁴ m³/C × 0.01 A × 0.2 T) / 1 × 10⁻⁴ m.
   3. Numerator: 3.8 × 10⁻⁴ × 0.01 × 0.2 = 7.6 × 10⁻⁷; divided by 1 × 10⁻⁴ m this gives 7.6 × 10⁻³ V = 7.6 mV.
   4. (b) Sensitivity S = VH / B = 7.6 × 10⁻³ V / 0.2 T = 0.038 V/T = 38 mV/T (equal to RH I / t at this current).
   Answer: The Hall voltage is 7.6 mV, and the sensitivity is 38 mV per tesla at 10 mA control current. */
