/* book Worked example 2: Q: The InSb plate of the first example (sensitivity 38 mV/T at 10 mA) sits in a 2 mm air gap of a ferrite ring clamped around a cable carrying 50 A DC. (a) Find the gap flux density. (b) Find the Hall voltage. (c) An amplifier of gain 500 follows the plate. Find the output and the scale in mV per ampere.
   1. Data: I = 50 A, g = 2 mm = 2 × 10⁻³ m, μ0 = 4π × 10⁻⁷ H/m, S = 38 mV/T = 0.038 V/T.
   2. (a) B = μ0 I / g = 4π × 10⁻⁷ × 50 / 2 × 10⁻³ = 6.283 × 10⁻⁵ / 2 × 10⁻³ = 0.0314 T = 31.4 mT.
   3. (b) VH = S B = 0.038 V/T × 0.0314 T = 1.19 × 10⁻³ V = 1.19 mV.
   4. (c) Vout = 500 × 1.19 mV = 0.597 V. Scale = 0.597 V / 50 A = 11.9 mV per ampere.
   Answer: The gap field is 31.4 mT, the Hall voltage 1.19 mV, and the amplified output 0.597 V, a scale of 11.9 mV/A. */
